<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6892" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cartēĭa</span></b> , ae,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καρτηία</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A very ancient seaport town in</i> Hispania
			Baetica, now near <i>Rocadillo</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 6,
			9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 1, 3, § 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Att.
				12, 44, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 28, 30, 3 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">43, 3,
			3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			Hence the <i>adjj.</i>, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Car-tēĭānus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>Carteian</i>, <i>of
				Carteia</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ora,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					3, 2, 3, § 17</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cartēĭensis</span></b> , e, the
			same: legati, Auct. B. Hisp. 36; <i>absol.</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 43, 3,
				4</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The chief town of the Olcades</i>, <i>in</i> Hispania Tarraconensis (acc. to others,
			Cartăla), <i><span class="en">Liv. 21, 5, 4</span></i>; cf. Alschefski ad h.
			l.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
